<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Griffin yr shr jumps, div increased.</title>
<headline>Griffin yr shr jumps, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		    133.3	    vs    43.0</p>
<p>    - cash			127.3	    vs    91.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   18.0	     vs    12.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     99.97	    vs    32.25</p>
<p>    Translation gain	  70.40	    vs    5.99</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     113.47	   vs    33.89</p>
<p>Tax</p>
<p>    - on operations	   2.59 received  vs    1.64 paid</p>
<p>    - on translation gain   16.08	    vs    nil</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     26.50	    vs    18.02</p>
<p>    Turnover		    239.63	   vs    172.75</p>
<p>Div payable February 24</p>
<p>on register February 14</p>
<p>Full name: Griffin Shipping Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the translation gain, which represents the increase in rand value of the net investment in U.S. dollar based assets, was particularly significant because of the depreciation of the rand against the U.S. dollar.</p>
<p>It said should the increased rand values be realised on the future disposal of the ships liable to South African tax then taxation of 16 million could arise. Provision has been made for this deferred tax on the translation gain.</p>
<p>It said the outlook for 1997 remained uncertain because of expectations of limited world trade growth and surplus capacity in the container ship and bulk carrier market.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
